        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "M.9 NOTE: M.9 is the backbone of modern intensive apple orchards worldwide.\n  High-density planting: 800–1,200 trees/acre (vs. 40–100 on seedling).\n  Each tree smaller; total yield per acre higher.\n  But: requires stake/wire trellis system (roots too weak to anchor alone).\n  The economics work because: precocity (bear in year 2–3 vs. year 7–10),\n  ease of harvest, fruit quality (better light penetration), labor efficiency.\n```"
    },
