      "text": "### Whip-and-Tongue (Splice Graft)"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#026",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:horticulture:02-grafting, git-history:horticulture:02-grafting]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "concepts": "[grafting]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:grafting",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[grafting]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nWHIP-AND-TONGUE GRAFT:\n  Best for: scion and rootstock of same or similar diameter (6–12mm)\n  Used for: bench grafting (done off the tree, indoors in winter)\n            grapes, ornamental trees, rootstock production"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#027",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:horticulture:02-grafting, git-history:horticulture:02-grafting]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "concepts": "[grafting]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:grafting",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[grafting]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CUT PROFILE:\n  1. Make 45° cut through both scion and rootstock\n  2. Make second cut to create interlocking tongue:\n     From midpoint of first cut, cut parallel to grain direction\n     halfway into the wood."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#028",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:horticulture:02-grafting, git-history:horticulture:02-grafting]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "concepts": "[grafting]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:grafting",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[grafting]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Scion:           Rootstock:\n      |\\               / |\n      | \\             / |\n      |  \\====       |  |\n      |   |   \\===== |  |\n      |   /   /      |  |\n      |  / ==|        \\ |\n      | /    \\         \\ |\n      |/      |"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#029",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:horticulture:02-grafting, git-history:horticulture:02-grafting]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "concepts": "[grafting]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:grafting",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[grafting]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "3. Interlock the tongues: the T-shape of scion fits into rootstock's slot.\n     Cambium layers must align on at least one side (preferably both).\n  4. Bind with grafting tape or parafilm.\n  5. Seal with wax or leave parafilm as sealer."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#030",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:horticulture:02-grafting, git-history:horticulture:02-grafting]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "concepts": "[grafting]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:grafting",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[grafting]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CAMBIUM ALIGNMENT IS CRITICAL:\n  If scion diameter ≠ rootstock diameter: align ONE side only.\n  The cambium is only 1–2 cells thick just inside the bark.\n  \"Line up the bark\" is the practical instruction.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#031",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
