      "text": "### Cleft Graft (for Top-working)"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#032",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:horticulture:02-grafting, git-history:horticulture:02-grafting]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "concepts": "[grafting]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:grafting",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[grafting]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCLEFT GRAFT:\n  Best for: topworking mature trees (replacing variety in old tree),\n            large rootstock much bigger than scion\n  Used for: re-grafting existing fruit trees to new varieties"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#033",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:horticulture:02-grafting, git-history:horticulture:02-grafting]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "concepts": "[grafting]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:grafting",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[grafting]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PROCEDURE:\n  1. Saw off branch cleanly (any size, typically 20–80mm diameter).\n  2. Split the stub through the center with cleaving tool.\n  3. Wedge open the split with tool left in place.\n  4. Prepare two scions: 6–8cm with 2–3 buds; base cut as\n     thin wedge (outer side slightly thicker than inner).\n  5. Insert one scion each side of split, cambium aligned.\n  6. Remove wedge from split; clamping action holds scions.\n  7. Wax all cut surfaces."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#034",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:horticulture:02-grafting, git-history:horticulture:02-grafting]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "concepts": "[grafting]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:grafting",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[grafting]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RESULT: Typically both scions take initially.\n  After 1 season: remove the weaker; leave strongest."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-GRAFTING.md#035",
      "path": [
        "02-GRAFTING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:horticulture:02-grafting, git-history:horticulture:02-grafting]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "concepts": "[grafting]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/02-GRAFTING.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:grafting",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[grafting]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grafting and Budding Techniques",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TIMING: Late dormant season (buds just swelling).\n          Rootstock must be actively beginning to grow;\n          scion must still be fully dormant.\n          \"Scion dormant, rootstock active\" = optimal.\n```"
    },
    {
